{
  "id": "Compound::DB00823 - Gene::5241",
  "verbalization": "Ethynodiol is closely related to progestin compounds through the class of Progesterone Congeners, which includes Norelgestromin, Norgestimate, and Megestrol Acetate. These compounds all bind to the Pgr receptor, suggesting a shared mechanism of action. The lowest common ancestor of Ethynodiol and these progestin-derived molecules is the Steroid class, indicating a common biological pathway. The evidence suggests that Ethynodiol may interact with Pgr through a mechanism involving progestin-like compounds, possibly by modulating receptor activity or influencing downstream signaling pathways. The consistent binding of these progestin congeners to Pgr, along with their shared ancestry, supports the hypothesis that Ethynodiol could exert a similar effect on Pgr, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
